0,Gbe languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gbe_languages,"Greenberg, following Westermann (1952), placed the Gbe languages in the Kwa family of the Niger–Congo languages. [2] The extent of the Kwa branch has fluctuated through the years, and Roger Blench places the Gbe languages in a Volta–Niger branch with former East Kwa languages to their east. Gbe is a dialect continuum. Based on comparative research, Capo (1988) divides it into five clusters ...","Gbe, Eastern Xwla",Niger-Congo
1,"Gbe, Eastern Xwla in Benin people group profile | Joshua ProjectGbe, Eastern Xwla in Benin Profile - joshuaproject.netBaba yabo, goun, gunbge etc. - YouTubeChiké & Mohbad - Egwu (Official Video) - YouTubeGbe, Eastern Xwla Language (GBX) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status ...Gbe languages - WikipediaNiger-Congo - playlist by Music League | Spotify",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/19585/BN,"Introduction / History The Eastern Xwla Gbe people are an indigenous ethnic community residing along the southeastern coastal region of Benin, particularly around the Ouémé and Atlantique departments near Cotonou. Their primary language, Gbe, Eastern Xwla, belongs to the larger Niger-Congo family and is part of the diverse cluster of Gbe languages spoken across southern Benin, Togo, and ... Their primary language, Gbe, Eastern Xwla, belongs to the larger Niger-Congo family and is part of the diverse cluster of Gbe languages spoken across southern Benin, Togo, and neighboring areas. It is a stable first language used across generations and remains central to the community's cultural identity. Mahuton speaking Fon, Gun, and Eastern Xwla | Niger-Congo languages | Wikitongues Wikitongues • 8.2K views • 5 years ago CREDITS: Songwriters - Osebuka Chike-Ezekpeazu, Ilerioluwa Oladimeji Aloba Song Producer - DeeYasso Video Director - Director Pink for Pinkline Films LYRICS: Imolenization Chike fun won ni ... Eastern Xwla Gbe is a stable indigenous language of Benin. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools. Greenberg, following Westermann (1952), placed the Gbe languages in the Kwa family of the Niger–Congo languages. [2] The extent of the Kwa branch has fluctuated through the years, and Roger Blench places the Gbe languages in a Volta–Niger branch with former East Kwa languages to their east. Gbe is a dialect continuum. Based on comparative research, Capo (1988) divides it into five clusters ... Playlist · Niger-Congo · 22 items · 4 saves Cookies, device or similar online identifiers together with other information (e.g. browser type and information, language, screen size, supported technologies, etc.) can be stored or read on your device to recognise it each time it connects to an app or to a website, for one or several of the purposes presented here.","Gbe, Eastern Xwla",Niger-Congo
